[68.85406, "o", "arXiv:0905.4129v3 [math-ph] 7 Jul 2009\r\n\r\nPerturbations of the Kerr black hole in the\r\nclass of axisymmetric artificial black holes.\r\nG.Eskin, Department of Mathematics, UCLA,\r\nLos Angeles, CA 90095-1555, USA. E-mail: eskin@math.ucla.edu\r\nNovember 20, 2018\r\nAbstract\r\nArtificial black holes (called also acoustic or optical black holes)\r\nare the black holes for the linear wave equation describing the wave\r\npropagation in a moving medium. They attracted a considerable interest of physicists who study them to better understand the black\r\nholes in general relativity. We consider the case of stationary axisymmetric metrics and we show that the Kerr black hole is not stable\r\nunder perturbations in the class of all axisymmetric metrics. We describe families of axisymmetric metrics having black holes that are\r\nthe perturbations of the Kerr black hole. We also show that the ergosphere can be determined by boundary measurements and we prove"]
[68.854442, "o", "\r\nthe uniform boundness of the solution in the exterior of the black hole\r\nwhen the event horizon coincides with the ergosphere.\r\n\r\n1\r\n\r\nIntroduction.\r\n\r\nConsider the wave equation:\r\n\r\n(1.1)\r\n\r\nn\r\nX\r\n\r\n∂\r\np\r\nn\r\n(−1) g(x) ∂xj\r\nj,k=0\r\n1\r\n\r\n\u0012\r\np\r\n"]
[68.854653, "o", "\r\n∂u(x0 , x)\r\n(−1)n g(x)g (x)\r\n∂xk\r\njk\r\n\r\n"]
[68.854742, "o", "\u0013\r\n\r\n=0\r\n\r\nin Ω × R, where Ω is a smooth bounded domain in Rn , x0 ∈ R is the time\r\nvariable, g(x) = det[gjk (x)]nj,k=0, [gjk (x)]nj,k=0 = ([g jk (x)]nj,k=0)−1 is a pseudoRiemanian metric with the Lorentz signature (1, −1, ..., −1). We assume that\r\n1\r\n\r\n\fg jk (x) are independent of x0 and smooth in Ω. We also assume that\r\ng 00 (x) > 0, ∀x ∈ Ω.\r\n\r\n(1.2)\r\n\r\nEquation (1.1) describes the wave propagation in a moving medium. We\r\nshall give two examples:\r\n1) The equation of propagation of light in a moving dielectric medium\r\n(the Gordon equation, cf. [G], [LP]). In this case the metric has the form:\r\n(1.3)\r\n\r\ngjk (x) = ηjk + (n−2 (x) − 1)vj vk , 0 ≤ j, k ≤ 3,\r\n\r\nwhere ηjk is the Lorenz metric tensor, η00 = 1, ηjj = −1, 1 ≤ j ≤ 3,\r\n\u0011− 21\r\n\u0010\r\np\r\n|w(x)|2\r\nηjk = 0, j 6= k, n(x) = ε(x)µ(x) is the refraction index, v0 (x) = 1 − c2\r\n,\r\n1\r\n\u0010\r\n\u0011\r\n2 −2 w\r\nj\r\n"]
[68.855063, "o", "vj (x) = − 1 − |w(x)|\r\n, 1 ≤ j ≤ 3, is the four-velocity, w(x) =\r\nc2\r\nc\r\n"]
